<title>USA: GM could up divs and begin buyback Monday - WSJ.</title>
<headline>GM could up divs and begin buyback Monday - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp could raise its dividend and begin a huge stock repurchase plan Monday, the Wall Street Journal said Friday.</p>
<p>Because both moves have been anticipated by so many, some analysts think the company's stock could fall if neither happens, the report said.</p>
<p>The paper said Ron Glantz, an analyst at Dean Witter, is predicting a buyback of $3 billion, which at the current price of the company's stock, would cut GM's outstanding shares by about six percent.</p>
<p>Most analysts think the nation's No. 1 auto maker will raise its quarterly dividend by $0.10 per share to $0.50, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
